# Length-framed proof/verdict data files are byte-exact: `entry <byte-len>`
# rows and the schema header are LF-anchored, and the file is embedded verbatim
# via `include_str!`. Git's autocrlf must NOT rewrite these to CRLF, or the
# embedded tier-0 verdict DB fails to parse on Windows (schema-line mismatch +
# corrupted length framing), silently disabling the proof cache.
*.vdb binary
# The include_str!-embedded LRAT canary certificates and their manifest are
# length-framed (`cnf <len>` / `drat <len>` / `smt2 <len>`) and SHA-256-pinned
# by canary_certs/manifest.v1 for exactly the same reason.
*.lratcert binary
crates/trust-cg-verify/verdict_db/canary_certs/manifest.v1 binary
# The bound-memory form certificates are committed zstd-compressed and their
# manifest is include_str!-embedded and SHA-256-bound into the replay
# authority's identity (verdict_db/README.md, "Bound-memory form certificates").
*.lratcert.zst binary
crates/trust-cg-verify/verdict_db/bound_memory_certs/manifest.v1 binary
crates/trust-cg-verify/verdict_db/atomic_memory_certs/manifest.v1 binary
crates/trust-cg-verify/verdict_db/neon_memory_certs/manifest.v1 binary
# The x86 split-copy replay fixtures are embedded with include_bytes! and
# SHA-256-pinned by their README (tests/e2e_x86_64_split_copy_replay.rs), so no
# checkout may rewrite their line endings.
crates/trust-cg-codegen/tests/fixtures/x86_split_copy_replay/* -text
